<title>GERMANY: Buba's Hesse against discount rate cut to 1.0 pct.</title>
<headline>Buba's Hesse against discount rate cut to 1.0 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HANOVER, Germany 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank council member Helmut Hesse said on Tuesday he was opposed to a reduction in German's discount rate to one percent from its 2.50 percent current level, as demanded by some politicians.</p>
<p>Hesse told journalists at an event in the town of Hanover that such a rate would not be in accord with the Bundesbank's 1997 and 1998 money supply targets and could have negative implications for the mark.</p>
<p>&quot;I would be concerned about the reaction of the financial markets (to such a move),&quot; he said.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
